+/*
+ * 0191: scan-out flip instead of a CPU copy a frame (boot-arg a8flip,
+ * default 1; console "flip 0|1").
+ *
+ * Every swap of CoreAnimation's second render target used to be memcpy'd
+ * into the panel memory: 9.6 MB a frame, in backboardd's SwapEnd.  The
+ * DT's reserved framebuffer@0xEC000000 is 20 MiB, enough for two
+ * 1080x2220 buffers, so backboardd's panel-sized BGRA render target (the
+ * one that is not the panel memory itself) gets the second half of it
+ * (sweet_fb_scanout_claim, from SweetSurface's create), and a swap just
+ * points DPP0's IDMA at whichever buffer was presented.  Registers, read
+ * live over the USB console on 2026-11-22 and moved by hand while the user
+ * watched the picture jump: IDMA G0 at 0x148b1000 (+0x10 SRC_SIZE =
+ * height << 16 | full width in pixels, +0x40 IN_BASE_ADDR_Y8 = 0xec000000),
+ * DECON_F 0x14860000 +0x60 SHADOW_REG_UPDATE_REQ (bit 31 global, bit 3 =
+ * window 3, the DT's default_win; the bit clears when the next frame takes
+ * the new values).  The swap waits for that, at most 20 ms: CoreAnimation
+ * draws its next frame into the buffer that is no longer shown.
